describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1SalesFunnelCampaigns"} → {"operationId":"postV1SalesFunnelCampaigns","method":"POST","path":"/v1/sales-funnel-campaigns","summary":"Launch a sales funnel as one campaign (brand x offer x sales funnel)","description":"Proxy to campaign-service POST /sales-funnel-campaigns. A SALES FUNNEL CAMPAIGN (owner 2026-10-10) is brand x offer x sales funnel: it owns one unit (an ordinary campaign) per pipe of the funnel and is run or paused as a whole. Its money is the funnel's caps at billing (GET /v1/brands/{brandId}/offers/{offerId}/sales-funnels/{salesFunnelId}/caps); no max budget = held unfunded. The org is the authenticated one. Status and body (with `reason` on a refusal) relayed verbatim. HOW each pipe behaves is fixed by the funnel's plays (`<leg>@<channel>~<strategy id>` in the funnel id; see the Plays tag: tactic, strategy, play on a pipe, a funnel carrying it, a campaign on that funnel). To change a behaviour (for example replies that carry an offer document as an attachment), launch a campaign on a funnel carrying the right play, created with `status: stopped` until the client agrees. Body { brandId, offerId, salesFunnelId, status: ongoing | stopped } forwarded untouched. 201 when created, 200 for an existing identity.

Request body: documented from campaign-service POST /sales-funnel-campaigns, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

