describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1ContentPreviewEmailPrepare"} → {"operationId":"postV1ContentPreviewEmailPrepare","method":"POST","path":"/v1/content/preview-email/prepare","summary":"Get ready to write preview emails for a brand (fire and forget)","description":"Proxy to content-generation-service POST /preview-email/prepare. Starts, in the background, the brand read POST /v1/content/preview-email will need for this brand, so the first preview only waits for the model. Answers 202 at once with the downstream body and status forwarded as-is; idempotent per org + brand. The brand read is billed to the calling org. Body + response shapes are owned by the downstream service (today: body { brandId, offerId? }, response { brandId, status }).

